* [[Iman Vellani]] as [[Kamala Khan (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Kamala Khan / Ms. Marvel]]:<br />A teenage [[Mutant (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|mutant]] from [[Jersey City]] who wears a magical bangle that unlocks her ability to harness cosmic energy and create [[Solid light|hard light]] constructs. Vellani said Kamala was central to the series, with the creators describing her role as "the Frodo of the story" in reference to the character [[Frodo Baggins]] from [[J. R. R. Tolkien]]'s novel ''[[The Lord of the Rings]]'' (1954–55).<ref name="VellaniVoice" />
* [[Dominique Thorne]] as [[Riri Williams (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Riri Williams / Ironheart]]: A former [[Massachusetts Institute of Technology|MIT]] student and genius inventor from Chicago who created a suit of armor that rivals [[Iron Man's armor (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|the one]] built by [[Tony Stark (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Tony Stark / Iron Man]]<ref name="CastNov2024CBR" />
* [[Hailee Steinfeld]] as [[Kate Bishop (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Kate Bishop]]: A young woman who trained to become a master archer after being saved by Clint Barton as a child<ref name="CastNov2024CBR" />
* [[Kerry Condon]] as [[F.R.I.D.A.Y. (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|F.R.I.D.A.Y.]]: An [[artificial intelligence]] (AI) created by Stark<ref name="CastSuperHeroHype" />
* Kenna Ramsey as [[Okoye (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Okoye]]: A zombie and the former general of the [[Dora Milaje (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Dora Milaje]], [[Wakanda (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Wakanda]]'s all-female [[special forces]]<ref name="Ramsey" />
* [[Todd Williams (actor)|Todd Williams]] as [[Blade (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|<!--Do not add "Eric Brooks"; named was created for Wesley Snipes Blade, while MCU Blade has no confirmed civilian name.-->Blade Knight]]:<br />A [[half-vampire]] "daywalker" who hunts vampires and has become the avatar of Khonshu, [[Moon Knight (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Moon Knight]],<ref name="Williams" /><ref name="BladeKnightAliLikeness" /> following the death of the mantle's previous bearer, [[Marc Spector (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Marc Spector]].<ref name="MarcSpectorDead" /> Since becoming the avatar of Khonshu, Blade Knight no longer needs to consume blood.<ref name="EasterEggs" />
* [[Kari Wahlgren]] as [[Melina Vostokoff (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Melina Vostokoff]]: A seasoned spy and scientist trained in the [[Red Room (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Red Room]] as a [[Black Widows (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Black Widow]] who is a mother figure to Yelena Belova<ref name="CastSuperHeroHype" />
* [[Florence Pugh]] as [[Yelena Belova (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Yelena Belova]]: A highly skilled spy and assassin who was trained in the Red Room as a Black Widow<ref name="CastNov2024CBR" />
* [[David Harbour]] as [[Alexei Shostakov (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Alexei Shostakov / Red Guardian]]: The Soviet [[super soldier]] counterpart to [[Captain America]] and a father figure to Belova<ref name="CastNov2024CBR" />
<!-- End 101 credits -->
* [[Simu Liu]] as [[Shang-Chi (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Xu Shang-Chi]]:<br />A highly skilled martial artist who was trained at a young age to be an assassin by his father Xu Wenwu.<ref name="CastNov2024CBR" /> In the series, Shang-Chi was bitten by a zombie on his right arm, and so he uses the mystical [[Ten Rings (object)|Ten Rings]] to prevent the infection from spreading to the rest of his body.<ref name="ShangChiBitten" />
* [[Awkwafina]] as [[Katy Chen]]:<ref name="ProductionBrief" /> Shang-Chi's best friend and former co-worker as a hotel [[valet]]<ref name="CastNov2024CBR" /> who wields the Ten Rings alongside him<ref name="KatyTenRings" />
* [[Randall Park]] as [[Jimmy Woo (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Jimmy Woo]]: A former [[Federal Bureau of Investigation|FBI]] agent<ref name="CastNov2024CBR" />
* [[Feodor Chin]] as [[Xu Wenwu]]: Shang-Chi's father who is the leader of the [[Ten Rings (organization)|Ten Rings]] organization and the original wielder of the mystical Ten Rings<ref name="Chin" />
* [[Wyatt Russell]] as [[John Walker (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|John Walker]]: A former captain of the [[75th Ranger Regiment|U.S. Army Rangers]]<ref name="AdditionalCastAug2025" />
* Rama Vallury as [[Helmut Zemo (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Helmut Zemo]]: A [[Sokovia]]n [[baron]] and terrorist<ref name="CastSuperHeroHype" />
* [[Elizabeth Olsen]] as [[Wanda Maximoff (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Wanda Maximoff / Scarlet Witch / Red Queen / Queen of the Dead]]: A former [[Avengers (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Avenger]] turned zombie who can harness [[chaos magic]], engage in [[telepathy]] and [[telekinesis]], and alter reality<ref name="CastNov2024CBR" /><ref name="ProductionBrief" />
<!-- End 102 credits -->
* [[Hudson Thames]] as [[Peter Parker (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Peter Parker / Spider-Man]]: A young man who received spider-like abilities after being bitten by a radioactive spider<ref name="Thames" />
* [[Paul Rudd]] as [[Scott Lang (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Scott Lang / Ant-Man]]:<br />A former petty criminal and superhero. The character's still-living head was preserved in a jar after he lost his body in the same process that cured him of the infection, as depicted in the ''[[What If...? (TV series)|What If...?]]'' episode "[[What If... Zombies?!]]" (2021).<ref name="AdditionalCastAug2025" />
* Greg Furman as [[Thor (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Thor]]: The [[Asgard (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Asgardian]] god of thunder and a founding Avenger, based on the [[Norse mythology|Norse mythological]] deity [[Thor|of the same name]]<ref name="CastSuperHeroHype" />
* [[Adam Hugill]] as [[Rintrah (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Rintrah]]: A [[minotaur]]-like being from [[R'Vaal]] who is a former student at [[Kamar-Taj (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Kamar-Taj]]<ref name="CastSuperHeroHype" />
* Daniel Swain as the [[London Master]]: A [[Master of the Mystic Arts]]<ref name="CastSuperHeroHype" />
* [[Sheila Atim]] as [[Sara (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Sara]]: A Master of the Mystic Arts<ref name="CastSuperHeroHype" />
* [[Tessa Thompson]] as [[Valkyrie (Marvel Cinematic Universe character)|Valkyrie]]: The last surviving member of an [[Valkyrie (Marvel Cinematic Universe team)|all-female group]] of Asgardian warriors<ref name="AdditionalCastAug2025" />
* [[F. Murray Abraham]] and [[Piotr Michael]] as [[Khonshu (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Khonshu]]: The Egyptian god of the moon.<ref name="CastSuperHeroHype" /> Abraham voices Khonshu in the third episode while Michael voices Khonshu in the fourth episode.{{cn|date=October 2024}}
<!-- End 103 credits -->
* [[Zenobia Shroff]] as [[Muneeba Khan]]: Kamala's mother<ref name="CastSuperHeroHype" />
